# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages (applied to every response).
#
# CSP is scoped to exactly what the site loads: its own bundle, Google Fonts,
# data: URIs (the inline SVG chevron), and Cloudflare Web Analytics.
# 'unsafe-inline' is required for React's inline style attributes and the
# JSON-LD block; everything else is locked to same-origin. frame-ancestors +
# X-Frame-Options block clickjacking.
#
# ⚠️ CLOUDFLARE WEB ANALYTICS — do not remove these two allowances.
# Cloudflare Pages injects its beacon into the HTML at the edge, for browser
# requests only (curl will not show it; a real browser will). This CSP used to
# be script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' / connect-src 'self', which BLOCKED the
# injected beacon: the site collected zero analytics from launch until
# 2026-08-10, and every visitor got a CSP violation in their console. The two
# hosts below are what the beacon actually needs, verified by reading
# beacon.min.js itself:
#   - static.cloudflareinsights.com  serves beacon.min.js          (script-src)
#   - cloudflareinsights.com         /cdn-cgi/rum fallback POST    (connect-src)
# On a proxied zone the beacon prefers SAME-ORIGIN /cdn-cgi/rum, which 'self'
# already covers (confirmed live on isoride.app). The cross-origin host is the
# documented fallback, so both are allowed.
# Guarded by src/data/site-consistency.test.ts.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com
